<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SActionScript version="1" name="plugin_native_editor_survives_strip">

  <!-- fix/editor-ui-and-shortcuts, issue (a): a native plugin editor window
       used to close whenever the user clicked into the arrangement, and would
       often refuse to reopen at all afterwards.

       ROOT CAUSE: SPluginNativeEditor's constructor did `QDialog( parent )`
       with `parentForPosition` passed straight through as the real Qt
       ownership parent, and SPluginEffectStrip::openParamEditor() passes THE
       STRIP ITSELF as that parent. STrackDetailPanel::rebuildUI() runs
       `delete pluginStrip_` on every track selection change (a lane click, a
       clip click, or an explicit track switch all route through
       SStdMixer::setSelectedTrack), which took the editor down as a Qt CHILD
       of the strip — exactly the failure the class's own header comment says
       it exists to avoid. `restoreOpenEditors()` passes SMainWindow instead of
       the strip, which is why a RESTORED editor never showed this bug and only
       an Edit-button-opened one did.

       This case reproduces it headlessly with the new `open-via-strip` verb
       mode (spluginuitestactions.cpp): it opens through a THROWAWAY
       SPluginEffectStrip — the exact call openParamEditor() makes — then
       destroys that strip the way rebuildUI() destroys the real one. Watched
       FAILING on the pre-fix binary: expectOpen="1" read isOpenFor()==false
       (the window was gone), so the case failed at the very assertion this
       header exists to gate. Fixed by climbing to parentForPosition->window()
       — the durable top-level SMainWindow — before handing it to QDialog, so
       any transient caller (a strip, a dock panel) is safe to pass; SMainWindow
       itself and nullptr (the headless open path) both still work because
       window() on a window is itself and window() on nullptr is nullptr.

       The throwaway strip is parented to the REAL main window (found via
       QApplication::topLevelWidgets(), exactly like sclicklaneaction.cpp's
       own lookup), never to nullptr: production parents a strip under
       STrackDetailPanel, ultimately under SMainWindow, so the fix's
       `parentForPosition->window()` climb lands PAST the strip. A parentless
       strip IS its own window() — a top-level widget's window() is itself —
       so testing with nullptr would make the climb land right back on the
       strip and silently test the PRE-fix shape even on the post-fix binary;
       this was found by doing exactly that first and watching the case still
       fail on the FIXED binary.

       NOT gated here (see the PR body): that the SAME window instance survives
       — only the registry entry does, which is everything a script can
       observe without a real GUI event loop; the "does not reopen" half of the
       report, which this fix removes by construction (the window is never
       abruptly destroyed any more, so there is nothing left to fail to
       recreate) but which had no isolated repro to gate on its own; and
       whether a REAL plugin's window is still visually anchored above the main
       window after the reparent (hand-verify only, no display in this run). -->

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackIndex="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="0"/>

    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.gui"
                   name="Smaragd Test GUI" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>

    <!-- Open through a throwaway strip, exactly as the FX strip's Edit button
         does, then destroy that strip exactly as a track switch does. The
         editor must survive: this IS the bug. -->
    <plugin-native-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0"
                          action="open-via-strip" expectOpen="1"/>

    <!-- And it must still be reachable/open after a second such destroy — not
         a one-shot survival. -->
    <plugin-native-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0"
                          action="open-via-strip" expectOpen="1"/>

    <!-- Take the window down. An editor alive when its plugin is destroyed is
         a contract violation the CLAP backend logs as an error. -->
    <plugin-native-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" action="close" expectOpen="0"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
